    "Scouting Notes": "Supremely patient hitter\n Top of the order skills are there, but also would like to see him swing more often. Feels passive at times.\n Power hasn't really been coming along like you'd hope, but perhaps a few signs of XBH pop early in 2024\n Very fast, should be a pretty big base stealer.\n Playing a lot of centerfield to go along with 2B now. Very solid defender at both.\n Arm is not great, but is fine.",
    "Notes Updated 2": "8/21/2022",
    "Scouting Notes 2": "2022 Draft Report\n  Top of the order bat to ball skills.\n  Will be interesting to see if/how the power develops. Not a big guy, but could see some Sal Frelick type pop in his bat.\n  Very fast, should be a pretty big base stealer.\n  Defensively it sounds like he will likely be limited to second base on the infield, but should be solid there.\n  Arm doesn't sound great, which is why he likely is stuck at second.\n  Interesting profile that aligns with the type of player the Brewers have been drafting lately and having success with.\n  Off to a good first week or so, definitely one to follow.",
